#N canvas 270 120 764 519 12;
#X text 20 10 Example (not used by the app): placed_sound with paulstretch~ instead of array_player~. To use it \, copy it over placed_sound.pd. An uploaded sound placed in the world \, stretched with paulstretch~ (loops). The sound itself is an array pair in main.pd's [pd sound_bank]. JS sends "set <left> [<right>]" to <name>-whistle-sound. Each time the sound has played through \, it says so on <name>-whistle-sound-end (JS ends a play-once sound). The faster the player moves \, the less it is stretched (10x standing).;
#X obj 20 160 r \$1-whistle-sound;
#X obj 20 190 route set stretch;
#X obj 20 220 list prepend set;
#X obj 20 250 list trim;
#X msg 200 370 stretch \$1;
#X obj 20 410 paulstretch~;
#X obj 20 460 outlet~;
#X obj 100 460 outlet~;
#X obj 300 160 r whistle-player;
#X obj 300 190 route speed;
#X obj 300 250 expr 1.5 + 8.5 / (1 + max(0 \, $f1));
#X text 300 275 speed (tiles/s \, averaged over the last 10 values = about 0.8 s \, so it follows a little late) -> stretch between 10x (standing) and 1.5x: 0 -> 10 \, 1 -> 5.75 \, 1.5 (walking) -> 4.9 \, 4 -> 3.2;
#X obj 300 220 moving_average 10;
#X obj 300 460 s \$1-whistle-sound-end;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 2 1 5 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 6 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 6 1 8 0;
#X connect 6 2 14 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 0 13 0;
#X connect 11 0 5 0;
#X connect 13 0 11 0;
